  "rationale": "Both answers are valid for the cue. Indonesian bingung directly covers being unclear or not understanding, while Malaysian Malay keliru covers mistaken or confused understanding. The contrast is a preference/commonness distinction, not an exclusive lexical split: bingung also exists in Malaysian Malay. No false-friend contrast is applicable.",
